From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthukumar <muthukumardce@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Feb 2026 21:01:47 +0530
Subject: Fix fingerprint signal mismatches: colorDepth, history.length,
 SeededNoise

Three changes to reduce detectable differences between Electron and Chrome:

1. screen.colorDepth: Return 32 (RGBA) on Windows instead of 24 (RGB).
   Chrome's ScreenInfo.depth reports 32 on Windows; Electron's display
   info only reports 24. Add BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) guard in Screen::colorDepth()
   to clamp to 32, matching Chrome's native behavior.

2. history.length: Add lengthForBinding() override via IDL ImplementedAs.
   FalconBrowser's tab initialization accumulates history entries (up to
   kMaxSessionHistoryEntries=50) before the user page loads, causing
   history.length to report 50 instead of Chrome's 1 for a fresh page.
   The ForBinding hook returns 1 when session overrides are active,
   matching Chrome's behavior (fpjs reports length-1=0).

3. SeededNoise: Return 0.5 when seed is 0 so that (SeededNoise-0.5)*factor
   produces exactly zero noise when no seed is configured. Prevents
   unintended noise artifacts when a fingerprint category is disabled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/history.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/history.cc
index 835ec7e99c6cc5f5c8797a389f855ce455a777cd..871c646956db326efb343abfbf7e6b58c60a2101 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/history.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/history.cc
@@ -55,6 +55,7 @@
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/weborigin/security_origin.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/wtf/text/strcat.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/wtf/text/string_view.h"
+#include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/session_override_helpers.h"
 
 namespace blink {
 
@@ -107,6 +108,17 @@ unsigned History::length(ExceptionState& exception_state) const {
   return DomWindow()->GetFrame()->Client()->BackForwardLength();
 }
 
+unsigned History::lengthForBinding(ScriptState* script_state,
+                                   ExceptionState& exception_state) const {
+  auto* storage = GetSessionOverrideStorage(script_state);
+  if (storage && storage->override_master_seed.has_value() &&
+      !storage->IsOverrideDisabled("history.length")) {
+    // Chrome fresh page: history.length = 1. Return 1 to match.
+    return 1;
+  }
+  return length(exception_state);
+}
+
 ScriptValue History::state(ScriptState* script_state,
                            ExceptionState& exception_state) {
   return StateHelper(script_state, exception_state);
